{"id":"proprium.dominica-iii-adventus-evangelium","title":"Misérunt Iudǽi ab Ierosólymis","category":"proprium","section":"missa-catechumenorum","variant":"dominica-iii-adventus","sung":false,"st":"working-edition","ad":5,"adw":6,"about":{"pl":"Ewangelia III Niedzieli Adwentu. Poselstwo z Jerozolimy pyta trzy razy, a odpowiedzi Jana są coraz krótsze: nie jestem ja Chrystusem, nie jestem, nie. Dopiero potem mówi, kim jest, i mówi to słowami Izajasza. Betania z ostatniego zdania leży za Jordanem i nie jest tą pod Jerozolimą, w której mieszkały Marta i Maria.","en":"The gospel of the Third Sunday of Advent. The delegation from Jerusalem asks three times, and John's answers grow shorter each time: I am not the Christ, I am not, no. Only after that does he say who he is, and he says it in Isaias' words. The Bethania of the last sentence lies beyond the Jordan and is not the one near Jerusalem where Martha and Mary lived."},"ac":{"pl":[382,383],"en":[382,383]},"seg":[{"id":"s01","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w001","f":"In","l":"in","m":0,"h":"w003"},{"i":"w002","f":"illo","l":"ille","m":116},{"i":"w003","f":"témpore","l":"tempus","p":":","m":135},{"i":"w004","f":"Misérunt","l":"mitto","m":272},{"i":"w005","f":"Iudǽi","l":"Iudaeus","m":118},{"i":"w006","f":"ab","l":"a","m":0,"h":"w007","a":7},{"i":"w007","f":"Ierosólymis","l":"Ierosolyma","m":1},{"i":"w008","f":"sacerdótes","l":"sacerdos","m":152},{"i":"w009","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w010","f":"levítas","l":"levita","m":278},{"i":"w011","f":"ad","l":"ad","m":3,"h":"w012"},{"i":"w012","f":"Ioánnem","l":"Ioannes","p":",","m":162},{"i":"w013","f":"ut","l":"ut","m":15},{"i":"w014","f":"interrogárent","l":"interrogo","m":413},{"i":"w015","f":"eum","l":"is","p":":","m":36}],"tr":{"pl":"W owym czasie Żydzi wysłali z Jerozolimy kapłanów i lewitów do Jana, aby go zapytali:","en":"At that time the Jews sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem to John to ask him:"},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["w","owym","czasie","posłali","Żydzi","z","Jerozolimy","kapłanów","i","lewitów","do","Jana","aby","zapytali","go"],"en":["in","that","time","sent","the Jews","from","Jerusalem","priests","and","Levites","to","John","that","they might ask","him"]}},{"id":"s02","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w016","f":"Tu","l":"tu","m":143},{"i":"w017","f":"quis","l":"quis","m":18},{"i":"w018","f":"es","l":"sum","p":"?","m":191}],"tr":{"pl":"Kim ty jesteś?","en":"Who are you?"},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["ty","kim","jesteś"],"en":["you","who","are"]}},{"id":"s03","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w019","f":"Et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w020","f":"conféssus","l":"confiteor","m":171,"h":"w021"},{"i":"w021","f":"est","l":"sum","p":",","m":21},{"i":"w022","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w023","f":"non","l":"non","m":32},{"i":"w024","f":"negávit","l":"nego","p":":","m":28},{"i":"w025","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w026","f":"conféssus","l":"confiteor","m":171,"h":"w027"},{"i":"w027","f":"est","l":"sum","p":":","m":21},{"i":"w028","f":"Quia","l":"quia","m":15},{"i":"w029","f":"non","l":"non","m":32},{"i":"w030","f":"sum","l":"sum","m":172},{"i":"w031","f":"ego","l":"ego","m":143},{"i":"w032","f":"Christus","l":"Christus","p":".","m":60}],"tr":{"pl":"On wyznał, nie zaprzeczył, lecz wyznał: Nie jestem Chrystusem.","en":"He confessed and did not deny, but confessed: I am not the Christ."},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["i","wyznał","—","a","nie","zaprzeczył","i","wyznał","—","że","nie","jestem","ja","Chrystusem"],"en":["and","confessed","(has)","and","not","denied","and","confessed","(has)","that","not","am","I","the Christ"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w021":"Z „conféssus” (w020) tworzy perfectum czasownika deponentnego. Polszczyzna oddaje je jednym słowem i dla łacińskiego „est” nie ma osobnej komórki.","w027":"To samo złożone perfectum co przy pierwszym „conféssus”, powtórzone.","w028":"Wprowadza mowę niezależną, a nie zdanie podrzędne. Grecki oryginał stawia tu „hóti” przed cytatem, a łacina oddaje je słowo w słowo. Przekład je pomija, bo polszczyzna otwiera cytat dwukropkiem."},"en":{"w021":"With “conféssus” (w020) this forms the perfect of a deponent verb. English builds the same tense with an auxiliary, which this cell supplies.","w027":"The same compound perfect as at the first “conféssus”, repeated.","w028":"It opens direct speech rather than a subordinate clause. The Greek puts “hoti” before the quotation and the Latin renders it word for word. The translation drops it, because English opens a quotation with the colon alone."}}},{"id":"s04","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w033","f":"Et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w034","f":"interrogavérunt","l":"interrogo","m":407},{"i":"w035","f":"eum","l":"is","p":":","m":36},{"i":"w036","f":"Quid","l":"quis","m":287},{"i":"w037","f":"ergo","l":"ergo","p":"?","m":32},{"i":"w038","f":"Elías","l":"Elias","m":390,"a":7},{"i":"w039","f":"es","l":"sum","m":191},{"i":"w040","f":"tu","l":"tu","p":"?","m":143}],"tr":{"pl":"Zapytali go: Kim więc jesteś? Czy jesteś Eliaszem?","en":"They asked him: What then? Are you Elijah?"},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["i","zapytali","go","co","więc","Eliaszem","jesteś","ty"],"en":["and","they asked","him","what","then","Elias","are","you"]}},{"id":"s05","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w041","f":"Et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w042","f":"dixit","l":"dico","p":":","m":195},{"i":"w043","f":"Non","l":"non","m":32},{"i":"w044","f":"sum","l":"sum","p":".","m":172},{"i":"w045","f":"Prophéta","l":"propheta","m":390},{"i":"w046","f":"es","l":"sum","m":191},{"i":"w047","f":"tu","l":"tu","p":"?","m":143},{"i":"w048","f":"Et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w049","f":"respóndit","l":"respondeo","p":":","m":23},{"i":"w050","f":"Non","l":"non","p":".","m":32}],"tr":{"pl":"Odpowiedział: Nie jestem. Czy jesteś prorokiem? Odrzekł: Nie.","en":"He said: I am not. Are you the prophet? He answered: No."},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["i","rzekł","nie","jestem","prorokiem","jesteś","ty","i","odpowiedział","nie"],"en":["and","he said","not","I am","the prophet","are","you","and","he answered","no"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w045":"Łacina nie ma rodzajnika, więc sama nie rozstrzyga, czy pytają o jakiegoś proroka, czy o Proroka zapowiedzianego Mojżeszowi. Grecki oryginał ma rodzajnik określony i to jego czyta ta edycja. Polszczyzna nie ma rodzajników i nie potrafi tego rozróżnienia zapisać w samym słowie."},"en":{"w045":"Latin has no article, so by itself it cannot say whether they ask about a prophet or about the Prophet promised to Moses. The Greek behind it has the definite article, and this edition reads it so — the gloss says the prophet."}},"fc":{"pl":{"w045":[381]},"en":{"w045":[381]}}},{"id":"s06","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","w":[{"i":"w051","f":"Dixérunt","l":"dico","m":272},{"i":"w052","f":"ergo","l":"ergo","m":32},{"i":"w053","f":"ei","l":"is","p":":","m":244},{"i":"w054","f":"Quis","l":"quis","m":18},{"i":"w055","f":"es","l":"sum","p":",","m":191},{"i":"w056","f":"ut","l":"ut","m":15},{"i":"w057","f":"respónsum","l":"responsum","m":82},{"i":"w058","f":"demus","l":"do","m":89},{"i":"w059","f":"his","l":"hic","p":",","m":42},{"i":"w060","f":"qui","l":"qui","m":124},{"i":"w061","f":"misérunt","l":"mitto","m":272},{"i":"w062","f":"nos","l":"nos","p":"?","m":49},{"i":"w063","f":"Quid","l":"quis","m":189},{"i":"w064","f":"dicis","l":"dico","m":84},{"i":"w065","f":"de","l":"de","m":0,"h":"w066"},{"i":"w066","f":"te","l":"tu","m":131},{"i":"w067","f":"ipso","l":"ipse","p":"?","m":288}],"tr":{"pl":"Rzekli mu więc: Kim jesteś, abyśmy dali odpowiedź tym, którzy nas posłali? Co mówisz sam o sobie?","en":"They said therefore to him: Who are you, that we may give an answer to those who sent us? What do you say of yourself?"},"tc":{"pl":[380],"en":[140]},"g":{"pl":["rzekli","więc","mu","kim","jesteś","abyśmy","odpowi